{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1253114-some-cantrip-questions","id":1253114,"title":"Some cantrip questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-10T11:59:49-07:00","id":1253114,"title":"Some cantrip questions","content":"I don't have a lot of experience with Changeling, but I've been going over the book lately and a few things are unclear to me.<br /> <br /> 1) Does it always take an action just to activate a cantrip -- or two separate actions if you want to do a bunk and then cast the cantrip? (For that matter, <i>can</i> you do a cantrip without a bunk, if you're willing to roll against difficulty 8?) If I want to use Quicksilver (Wayfare 2) in a fight, do I have to spend one turn just activating the cantrip before I get extra actions on the next turn? (Please tell me I don't have to spend one turn doing a bunk, then a second casting the cantrip, and <i>then</i> get extra actions on round 3.)<br /> <br /> A lot of the Dragon's Ire powers, as well, seem like it would be very hard to make effective use of them if you have to spend 1-2 turns just casting the effect before you can enjoy its benefits in action. oWoD fights tend to go pretty fast.<br /> <br /> 2) Is there any guideline to the actual effects of Metamorphosis cantrips? Worms and Giants can make someone much bigger, but does it increase their Strength or soak? (If you make someone smaller, do they get any weaker?) Thousandskins, at least, says the target gains the physical traits of whatever they turn into (and I'm sure I can find oWoD stats for a lion somewhere). Beastskin is pretty vague about what mechanical effects it might have, though, and Chimeric Exultation in particular...well, you can turn the target into any damn thing you want, and they can have up to one &quot;fantastic ability&quot; per success.<br /> <br /> Obviously an ability this broad is going to involve a lot of Storyteller interpretation sooner or later, but it would be nice to have some general rule for what sort of dice bonus a &quot;fantastic ability&quot; can give you. Does anyone have thoughts on this one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T13:11:47-07:00","id":1253118,"title":"","content":"1) Bunks are not mandatory, but most would take at least an action to do.<br /> <br /> 2) I agree, Dragons Ire is very underpowered. I try to just steer my players away from it, and don't give it to NPCs.<br /> <br /> 3) I don't think Worms and Giants should affect soak or strength. For the others I don't think I understand the question really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T13:24:29-07:00","id":1253121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1253114-some-cantrip-questions?p=1253118#post1253118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) I don't think Worms and Giants should affect soak or strength. For the others I don't think I understand the question really.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question is &quot;what benefits (in terms of game mechanics) is a character supposed to gain from transforming into a mythic creature via Chimeric Exultation?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Each success allows the changeling to name one fantastic ability to be granted by the transformation (a dragon, for example, might possess flight, fantastic strength, fantastic toughness, and flaming breath).&quot; The book doesn't say (so far as I can tell) what any of these fantastic abilities might actually entail. How many dice is &quot;fantastic strength&quot; worth, for example?<br /> <br /> I'm really hoping there's a better answer than &quot;the Storyteller should just make something up.&quot; Is there a rule somewhere I missed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T13:32:24-07:00","id":1253122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1253114-some-cantrip-questions?p=1253121#post1253121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question is &amp;quot;what benefits (in terms of game mechanics) is a character supposed to gain from transforming into a mythic creature via Chimeric Exultation?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Each success allows the changeling to name one fantastic ability to be granted by the transformation (a dragon, for example, might possess flight, fantastic strength, fantastic toughness, and flaming breath).&amp;quot; The book doesn't say (so far as I can tell) what any of these fantastic abilities might actually entail. How many dice is &amp;quot;fantastic strength&amp;quot; worth, for example?<br /> <br /> I'm really hoping there's a better answer than &amp;quot;the Storyteller should just make something up.&amp;quot; Is there a rule somewhere I missed?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's the storyteller should make something up.<br /> <br /> I suspect you really won't like the Unleashing rules once you take a closer look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T13:59:50-07:00","id":1253128,"title":"","content":"Re: growing bigger. I'd give extra health levels, since the merit which makes you a large human gives you an extra health level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T14:06:12-07:00","id":1253129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1253114-some-cantrip-questions?p=1253122#post1253122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it's the storyteller should make something up.<br /> <br /> I suspect you really won't like the Unleashing rules once you take a closer look.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not especially fond of the Unleashing rules, but those bother me less than a specific, level-five power being either the strongest or weakest thing in the game depending on how the GM feels about you today.<br /> <br /> (I suppose that the effects of Chimeric Exultation wouldn't need to be immense to be worth using. At least you don't have to allocate successes to duration (like Dragon's Ire). But still.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T14:10:51-07:00","id":1253130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1253114-some-cantrip-questions?p=1253129#post1253129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not especially fond of the Unleashing rules, but those bother me less than a specific, level-five power being either the strongest or weakest thing in the game depending on how the GM feels about you today.<br /> <br /> (I suppose that the effects of Chimeric Exultation wouldn't need to be immense to be worth using. At least you don't have to allocate successes to duration (like Dragon's Ire). But still.)</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have a bad ST, you should leave the game. That's a basic assumption of all the White Wolf games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T15:09:52-07:00","id":1253149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1253114-some-cantrip-questions?p=1253130#post1253130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you have a bad ST, you should leave the game. That's a basic assumption of all the White Wolf games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but that's not really the point here. Even a good ST may be unsure of how to handle Chimeric Exultation, because when you have no real guidelines at all, it's very difficult to figure out what result would be fair to everyone at the table.<br /> <br /> Have any STs out there had a player use this cantrip? If so, how did you work it out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T23:37:10-07:00","id":1253222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1253114-some-cantrip-questions?p=1253149#post1253149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have any STs out there had a player use this cantrip? If so, how did you work it out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's use the powers of Bygone Bestiary.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T12:15:26-07:00","id":1253972,"title":"","content":"Time 3 is a great advantage for combat casting. It adds +1 difficulty but you can take your time with the bunk and even cast inside a freehold for an extra -1","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T13:12:28-07:00","id":1253985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daniel Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1253114-some-cantrip-questions?p=1253972#post1253972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time 3 is a great advantage for combat casting. It adds +1 difficulty but you can take your time with the bunk and even cast inside a freehold for an extra -1</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus if you're willing to spend an extra point if Glamour you don't even need to buy Time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.t